-- Fullbright: the originals (Lighting values, effect Enabled flags) are saved once when it turns on and put back when it turns off or on unload.
-- Blind detection, from your WrenchBlindWatch log of one Octopop blind: a ScreenGui named "inksplash" (with a LocalScript "inkeffect" and an
-- ImageLabel) appears in PlayerGui when the blind starts and is removed about 6 seconds later. Config.Blind.Detect is true while it exists.
-- Note: it is a GUI image overlay, so fullbright raises the lighting but does not remove the overlay itself.
Config.Blind = {
    GuiName = "inksplash",
    Detect = function()
        local pg = LocalPlayer:FindFirstChildOfClass("PlayerGui")
        local ink = pg and pg:FindFirstChild(Config.Blind.GuiName)
